{
  "content": {
    "items": [
      {
        "description": "No Edit/Write tools, no sed, no heredocs, no shell redirection into .pebbles/. The CLI validates and writes atomically; direct edits corrupt ids, refs and statuses. Reading spec files is always fine.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "e9514b09-f336-436b-91ab-15ef74cd2ba9",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Never create, edit or delete .pebble files directly"
      },
      {
        "description": "Ask the user where pebbles-cli lives — never fall back to editing files by hand.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "583de7c8-b731-49bd-b1b3-3158c97acebb",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "If the CLI is unavailable, treat the spec graph as read-only"
      },
      {
        "description": "Plain pebbles-cli calls are pre-approved and run without prompting. Mixing in other programs, && or | chaining, redirects, or $(…) forces a manual permission prompt.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "fe8ef5e3-bd0e-4ad5-a6b0-34805c9de43b",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Call the CLI purely — one binary, no chaining"
      },
      {
        "description": "Validation errors are written to be actionable: wrong status vocabularies list the allowed values, missing targets name the path, incomplete fields name the field.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "0bbcfc18-2b7b-48d2-af67-b3d79ae5de14",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "On an error, READ the message — it tells you the fix"
      },
      {
        "description": "Removing spec is a human decision made in the Pebbles app. Mark superseded things `deprecated` instead.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "38d2fd92-05dd-4ef2-8f79-3dce5a26a53b",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "There is deliberately no delete"
      }
    ],
    "kind": "checklist"
  },
  "createdAt": "2026-07-21T14:32:38.676Z",
  "description": "The spec graph is written ONLY through pebbles-cli. This is the prime rule of the platform — every other rule builds on it.",
  "id": "9ea65046-c8a8-4630-a0a1-b4cd40956a6b",
  "name": "Spec mutation contract",
